Package: eDNAstructure
Title: Dirichlet-Multinomial Mixture Models for eDNA Metabarcoding Community Structure
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Pedro", "Brandao-Dias", email = "pbdfp@uw.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits Bayesian Dirichlet-Multinomial Mixture (DMM) models to
    environmental DNA (eDNA) read count data from metabarcoding surveys. The
    model identifies latent ecological communities, estimates their taxonomic
    compositions, and quantifies how environmental covariates such as depth or
    latitude drive community membership. Inference is performed with Stan.
    Because a mixture likelihood is unchanged by permuting its components,
    chains can label the same communities differently; community labels are
    therefore aligned across draws automatically, and diagnostics are reported
    that distinguish disagreement about labels from disagreement about the
    grouping itself. Visualization functions produce publication-ready ggplot2
    objects for community structure plots, composition plots, NMDS ordinations
    and covariate coefficient plots.
